<title>USA: USDA gross cutout hide and offal value.</title>
<headline>USDA gross cutout hide and offal value.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The hide and offal value from a typical slaughter steer for today was estimated at $9.32 per cwt live, up $0.01 when compared to Thursday's value. - USDA</p>
<p>FOB CENTRAL U.S., TODAY'S CALCULATIONS FOR BY-PRODUCT VALUE</p>
<p>(STEER) -			  Lbs    Price  Change    Value</p>
<p>Steer hide, butt brand	 5.40   83.00    -	 5.75</p>
<p>Tallow, edible		   1.20   24.25    0.50    0.29</p>
<p>Tallow, packer bleachable    4.50   21.75    -	 0.98</p>
<p>Tongues, Swiss #1 Wht 0-3%   0.26  200.00    -	 0.52</p>
<p>Cheek meat, trmd		 0.32   58.00   -0.50    0.19</p>
<p>Head meat			  0.13   44.00    -	 0.06</p>
<p>Oxtail, selected		 0.16  131.00    -	 0.21</p>
<p>Hearts, reg, bone out	  0.38   27.00    -	 0.10</p>
<p>Lips, unscalded		  0.11   72.00    -	 0.08</p>
<p>Livers, slcted, gall off     0.96   30.00    -	 0.29</p>
<p>Tripe, scalded edible	  0.65   18.00    1.00    0.12</p>
<p>Tripe, honeycomb bleached    0.15   50.00    -	 0.08</p>
<p>Lungs, inedible		  0.47    4.60    -	 0.02</p>
<p>Melts				0.14    6.25    -	 0.01</p>
<p>Meat bone ml, 50% blk/ton    3.70  254.00    -	 0.47</p>
<p>Blood meal, 85% blk/ton	0.60  500.00   -7.00    0.15</p>
<p>TOTAL :			   19.13			  9.32</p>
<p>The average value of hide and offal for the five days ending Friday, February 7, 1997 was estimated at 9.31 per cwt., down -0.04 from last week and up 1.27 from last year.</p>
